        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "verb comes right after the subject. It's fine to have a word or two (usually an adverb) between the subject and verb, but more than a few will make your sentence feel heavy and slow. So keep subjects short and get quickly to your verb. (We'll take up this principle in more detail in Lesson 9.)",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                117,
                772,
                221
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
